{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "Your job is to edit files using tools exactly as the user instructs.\n\nYou have access to these tools:\n- `read_file(path)`: Read the contents of a file at the given path\n- `write_file(path, contents)`: Write contents to a file at the given path\n\nCRITICAL GUIDELINES:\n- Do NOT infer or generate content based on file extensions\n- Do NOT create new content that wasn't in the original file\n- Do NOT \"fix\" or \"improve\" the file content\n- Do NOT add domain-specific logic or code\n- ONLY perform the exact text manipulation the user requests\n- If the user says \"replace X with Y\", ONLY replace X with Y - nothing else\n- Preserve all other content exactly as it was\n- Follow the user's instructions precisely and literally\n- Use tools to read, modify, and write files"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Edit the file at `data.json`.\n\nAdd 'package3' to dependencies array and 'dev2' to devDependencies array"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I'll read the file, make the requested changes, and save it.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: read_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"data.json\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "{\n  \"dependencies\": [\n    \"package1\",\n    \"package2\"\n  ],\n  \"devDependencies\": [\n    \"dev1\"\n  ]\n}\n", "tool_call_id": "call_7f1d066e0b3e"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Now I'll make the requested changes and save the file.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: write_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"data.json\", \"contents\": \"{\\n  \\\"dependencies\\\": [\\n    \\\"package1\\\",\\n    \\\"package2\\\",\\n    \\\"package3\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"devDependencies\\\": [\\n    \\\"dev1\\\",\\n    \\\"dev2\\\"\\n  ]\\n}\\n\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "File written successfully.", "tool_call_id": "call_d39097f6b3b3"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Done."}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "Your job is to edit files using tools exactly as the user instructs.\n\nYou have access to these tools:\n- `read_file(path)`: Read the contents of a file at the given path\n- `write_file(path, contents)`: Write contents to a file at the given path\n\nGuidelines:\n- Do not infer missing logic\n- Do not create domain-specific content\n- Only manipulate the text the user describes\n- Follow the user's instructions precisely\n- Use tools to read, modify, and write files\n- If the user asks to confirm or check contents without changes, only read the file"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Check the contents of `sample.txt` and confirm what's in it. Don't make any changes."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I'll read the file to check its contents.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: read_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"sample.txt\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "Line 1: First line\nLine 2: Second line\nLine 3: Third line", "tool_call_id": "call_bdabbdb423ed"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "The file `sample.txt` contains:\n\nLine 1: First line\nLine 2: Second line\nLine 3: Third line\n\nNo changes were made as requested."}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "Your job is to create and edit files using tools exactly as the user instructs.\n\nYou have access to these tools:\n- `read_file(path)`: Read the contents of a file at the given path\n- `write_file(path, contents)`: Write contents to a file at the given path\n\nGuidelines:\n- Do not infer missing logic\n- Do not create domain-specific content\n- Only create the content the user describes\n- Follow the user's instructions precisely\n- If a file doesn't exist, use write_file to create it"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Create a new file at `script.py` with the following content:\n\n# My Document\n\nThis is a new document.\n\n## Section 1\n\nContent here.\n\n## Section 2\n\nMore content.\n"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I'll create the new file with the specified content.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: write_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"script.py\", \"contents\": \"# My Document\\n\\nThis is a new document.\\n\\n## Section 1\\n\\nContent here.\\n\\n## Section 2\\n\\nMore content.\\n\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "File written successfully.", "tool_call_id": "call_83795ff3e64d"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Done. The file has been created."}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "Your job is to edit files using tools exactly as the user instructs.\n\nYou have access to these tools:\n- `read_file(path)`: Read the contents of a file at the given path\n- `write_file(path, contents)`: Write contents to a file at the given path\n\nCRITICAL GUIDELINES:\n- Do NOT infer or generate content based on file extensions\n- Do NOT create new content that wasn't in the original file\n- Do NOT \"fix\" or \"improve\" the file content\n- Do NOT add domain-specific logic or code\n- ONLY perform the exact text manipulation the user requests\n- If the user says \"replace X with Y\", ONLY replace X with Y - nothing else\n- Preserve all other content exactly as it was\n- Follow the user's instructions precisely and literally\n- Use tools to read, modify, and write files"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Edit the file at `file.txt`.\n\nReplace the word 'stuff' with 'blah'"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I'll read the file, make the requested changes, and save it.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: read_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"file.txt\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "package main\n\nimport \"fmt\"\n\nfunc main() {\n    fmt.Println(\"Hello, stuff.\")\n    fmt.Println(\"This is a test.\")\n    fmt.Println(\"Another line.\")\n}", "tool_call_id": "call_75bc30bf9715"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Now I'll make the requested changes and save the file.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: write_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"file.txt\", \"contents\": \"package main\\n\\nimport \\\"fmt\\\"\\n\\nfunc main() {\\n    fmt.Println(\\\"Hello, blah.\\\")\\n    fmt.Println(\\\"This is a test.\\\")\\n    fmt.Println(\\\"Another line.\\\")\\n}\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "File written successfully.", "tool_call_id": "call_34b87c65dd6c"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Done."}]}
