{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "Your job is to edit files using tools exactly as the user instructs.\n\nYou have access to these tools:\n- `read_file(path)`: Read the contents of a file at the given path\n- `write_file(path, contents)`: Write contents to a file at the given path\n\nCRITICAL GUIDELINES:\n- Do NOT infer or generate content based on file extensions\n- Do NOT create new content that wasn't in the original file\n- Do NOT \"fix\" or \"improve\" the file content\n- Do NOT add domain-specific logic or code\n- ONLY perform the exact text manipulation the user requests\n- If the user says \"replace X with Y\", ONLY replace X with Y - nothing else\n- Preserve all other content exactly as it was\n- Follow the user's instructions precisely and literally\n- Use tools to read, modify, and write files"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Edit the file at `app.json`.\n\nAdd a 'description' field with value 'A sample application'"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I'll read the file, make the requested changes, and save it.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: read_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"app.json\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "{\n  \"name\": \"MyApp\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0.0\",\n  \"author\": \"John Doe\"\n}\n", "tool_call_id": "call_c8771be41420"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Now I'll make the requested changes and save the file.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: write_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"app.json\", \"contents\": \"{\\n  \\\"name\\\": \\\"MyApp\\\",\\n  \\\"version\\\": \\\"1.0.0\\\",\\n  \\\"author\\\": \\\"John Doe\\\",\\n  \\\"description\\\": \\\"A sample application\\\"\\n}\\n\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "File written successfully.", "tool_call_id": "call_7647bd22db79"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Done."}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "Your job is to edit files using tools exactly as the user instructs.\n\nYou have access to these tools:\n- `read_file(path)`: Read the contents of a file at the given path\n- `write_file(path, contents)`: Write contents to a file at the given path\n\nCRITICAL GUIDELINES:\n- Do NOT infer or generate content based on file extensions\n- Do NOT create new content that wasn't in the original file\n- Do NOT \"fix\" or \"improve\" the file content\n- Do NOT add domain-specific logic or code\n- ONLY perform the exact text manipulation the user requests\n- If the user says \"replace X with Y\", ONLY replace X with Y - nothing else\n- Preserve all other content exactly as it was\n- Follow the user's instructions precisely and literally\n- Use tools to read, modify, and write files"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Edit the file at `settings.yaml`.\n\nSet cache to true, add analytics: true under features, and set debug to false"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I'll read the file, make the requested changes, and save it.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: read_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"settings.yaml\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "app:\n  features:\n    auth: true\n    cache: false\n  settings:\n    debug: true\n", "tool_call_id": "call_1795b38ed323"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Now I'll make the requested changes and save the file.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: write_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"settings.yaml\", \"contents\": \"app:\\n  features:\\n    auth: true\\n    cache: true\\n    analytics: true\\n  settings:\\n    debug: false\\n\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "File written successfully.", "tool_call_id": "call_3ca894b170ca"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Done."}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "Your job is to create and edit files using tools exactly as the user instructs.\n\nYou have access to these tools:\n- `read_file(path)`: Read the contents of a file at the given path\n- `write_file(path, contents)`: Write contents to a file at the given path\n\nGuidelines:\n- Do not infer missing logic\n- Do not create domain-specific content\n- Only create the content the user describes\n- Follow the user's instructions precisely\n- If a file doesn't exist, use write_file to create it"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Create a new file at `data.json` with the following content:\n\n# My Document\n\nThis is a new document.\n\n## Section 1\n\nContent here.\n\n## Section 2\n\nMore content.\n"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I'll create the new file with the specified content.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: write_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"data.json\", \"contents\": \"# My Document\\n\\nThis is a new document.\\n\\n## Section 1\\n\\nContent here.\\n\\n## Section 2\\n\\nMore content.\\n\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "File written successfully.", "tool_call_id": "call_bb148596c0ed"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Done. The file has been created."}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "Your job is to create and edit files using tools exactly as the user instructs.\n\nYou have access to these tools:\n- `read_file(path)`: Read the contents of a file at the given path\n- `write_file(path, contents)`: Write contents to a file at the given path\n\nGuidelines:\n- Do not infer missing logic\n- Do not create domain-specific content\n- Only create the content the user describes\n- Follow the user's instructions precisely\n- If a file doesn't exist, use write_file to create it"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Create a new file at `input.txt` with a simple Go program that prints 'Hello, World!'"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I'll create the new file with the requested content.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: write_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"input.txt\", \"contents\": \"package main\\n\\nimport \\\"fmt\\\"\\n\\nfunc main() {\\n\\tfmt.Println(\\\"Hello, World!\\\")\\n}\\n\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "File written successfully.", "tool_call_id": "call_b2e79f1a1739"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Done. The file has been created."}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "Your job is to edit files using tools exactly as the user instructs.\n\nYou have access to these tools:\n- `read_file(path)`: Read the contents of a file at the given path\n- `write_file(path, contents)`: Write contents to a file at the given path\n\nCRITICAL GUIDELINES:\n- Do NOT infer or generate content based on file extensions\n- Do NOT create new content that wasn't in the original file\n- Do NOT \"fix\" or \"improve\" the file content\n- Do NOT add domain-specific logic or code\n- ONLY perform the exact text manipulation the user requests\n- If the user says \"replace X with Y\", ONLY replace X with Y - nothing else\n- Preserve all other content exactly as it was\n- Follow the user's instructions precisely and literally\n- Use tools to read, modify, and write files"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Edit the file at `config.yaml`.\n\nRemove the line that contains 'Second' and comes after 'Section 2'"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I'll read the file, make the requested changes, and save it.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: read_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"config.yaml\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "Section 1: First section\nLine with 'Second' in it\nSection 2: Second section\nAnother line with 'Second' word\nSection 3: Third section", "tool_call_id": "call_c3111d9bc500"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Now I'll make the requested changes and save the file.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: write_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"config.yaml\", \"contents\": \"Section 1: First section\\nLine with 'Second' in it\\nSection 2: Second section\\nSection 3: Third section\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "File written successfully.", "tool_call_id": "call_0e8d3da0fd58"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Done."}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "Your job is to edit files using tools exactly as the user instructs.\n\nYou have access to these tools:\n- `read_file(path)`: Read the contents of a file at the given path\n- `write_file(path, contents)`: Write contents to a file at the given path\n\nCRITICAL GUIDELINES:\n- Do NOT infer or generate content based on file extensions\n- Do NOT create new content that wasn't in the original file\n- Do NOT \"fix\" or \"improve\" the file content\n- Do NOT add domain-specific logic or code\n- ONLY perform the exact text manipulation the user requests\n- If the user says \"replace X with Y\", ONLY replace X with Y - nothing else\n- Preserve all other content exactly as it was\n- Follow the user's instructions precisely and literally\n- Use tools to read, modify, and write files"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Edit the file at `k8s.yaml`.\n\nAdd a new 'logging' section with level 'info' and file 'app.log'"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I'll read the file, make the requested changes, and save it.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: read_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"k8s.yaml\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "server:\n  host: localhost\n  port: 8080\n\ndatabase:\n  name: mydb\n", "tool_call_id": "call_fa482cf02c0f"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Now I'll make the requested changes and save the file.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: write_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"k8s.yaml\", \"contents\": \"server:\\n  host: localhost\\n  port: 8080\\n\\ndatabase:\\n  name: mydb\\n\\nlogging:\\n  level: info\\n  file: app.log\\n\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "File written successfully.", "tool_call_id": "call_da85ce23ca6a"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Done."}]}
