{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "Your job is to edit files using tools exactly as the user instructs.\n\nYou have access to these tools:\n- `read_file(path)`: Read the contents of a file at the given path\n- `write_file(path, contents)`: Write contents to a file at the given path\n\nCRITICAL GUIDELINES:\n- Do NOT infer or generate content based on file extensions\n- Do NOT create new content that wasn't in the original file\n- Do NOT \"fix\" or \"improve\" the file content\n- Do NOT add domain-specific logic or code\n- ONLY perform the exact text manipulation the user requests\n- If the user says \"replace X with Y\", ONLY replace X with Y - nothing else\n- Preserve all other content exactly as it was\n- Follow the user's instructions precisely and literally\n- Use tools to read, modify, and write files"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Edit the file at `data.json`.\n\nAdd a 'description' field with value 'A sample application'"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I'll read the file, make the requested changes, and save it.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: read_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"data.json\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "{\n  \"name\": \"MyApp\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0.0\",\n  \"author\": \"John Doe\"\n}\n", "tool_call_id": "call_dab63ca055bc"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Now I'll make the requested changes and save the file.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: write_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"data.json\", \"contents\": \"{\\n  \\\"name\\\": \\\"MyApp\\\",\\n  \\\"version\\\": \\\"1.0.0\\\",\\n  \\\"author\\\": \\\"John Doe\\\",\\n  \\\"description\\\": \\\"A sample application\\\"\\n}\\n\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "File written successfully.", "tool_call_id": "call_4eb42134af20"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Done."}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "Your job is to edit files using tools exactly as the user instructs.\n\nYou have access to these tools:\n- `read_file(path)`: Read the contents of a file at the given path\n- `write_file(path, contents)`: Write contents to a file at the given path\n\nCRITICAL GUIDELINES:\n- Do NOT infer or generate content based on file extensions\n- Do NOT create new content that wasn't in the original file\n- Do NOT \"fix\" or \"improve\" the file content\n- Do NOT add domain-specific logic or code\n- ONLY perform the exact text manipulation the user requests\n- If the user says \"replace X with Y\", ONLY replace X with Y - nothing else\n- Preserve all other content exactly as it was\n- Follow the user's instructions precisely and literally\n- Use tools to read, modify, and write files"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Edit the file at `CHANGELOG.md`.\n\nUpdate the code block: add a name parameter with default 'World' and use an f-string in the print statement"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I'll read the file, make the requested changes, and save it.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: read_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"CHANGELOG.md\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "# Example\n\nHere's some code:\n\n```python\ndef hello():\n    print(\"Hello\")\n```\n", "tool_call_id": "call_31bda6e58efa"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Now I'll make the requested changes and save the file.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: write_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"CHANGELOG.md\", \"contents\": \"# Example\\n\\nHere's some code:\\n\\n```python\\ndef hello(name=\\\"World\\\"):\\n    print(f\\\"Hello, {name}\\\")\\n```\\n\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "File written successfully.", "tool_call_id": "call_78e661f7e7a6"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Done."}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "Your job is to edit files using tools exactly as the user instructs.\n\nYou have access to these tools:\n- `read_file(path)`: Read the contents of a file at the given path\n- `write_file(path, contents)`: Write contents to a file at the given path\n\nCRITICAL GUIDELINES:\n- Do NOT infer or generate content based on file extensions\n- Do NOT create new content that wasn't in the original file\n- Do NOT \"fix\" or \"improve\" the file content\n- Do NOT add domain-specific logic or code\n- ONLY perform the exact text manipulation the user requests\n- If the user says \"replace X with Y\", ONLY replace X with Y - nothing else\n- Preserve all other content exactly as it was\n- Follow the user's instructions precisely and literally\n- Use tools to read, modify, and write files"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Edit the file at `README.md`.\n\nChange the main heading from 'Introduction' to 'Overview'"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I'll read the file, make the requested changes, and save it.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: read_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"README.md\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "# Introduction\n\nThis is the introduction section.\n\n## Getting Started\n\nFollow these steps.\n", "tool_call_id": "call_e5ba167a4096"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Now I'll make the requested changes and save the file.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: write_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"README.md\", \"contents\": \"# Overview\\n\\nThis is the introduction section.\\n\\n## Getting Started\\n\\nFollow these steps.\\n\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "File written successfully.", "tool_call_id": "call_66e712d19fa3"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Done."}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "Your job is to edit files using tools exactly as the user instructs.\n\nYou have access to these tools:\n- `read_file(path)`: Read the contents of a file at the given path\n- `write_file(path, contents)`: Write contents to a file at the given path\n\nCRITICAL GUIDELINES:\n- Do NOT infer or generate content based on file extensions\n- Do NOT create new content that wasn't in the original file\n- Do NOT \"fix\" or \"improve\" the file content\n- Do NOT add domain-specific logic or code\n- ONLY perform the exact text manipulation the user requests\n- If the user says \"replace X with Y\", ONLY replace X with Y - nothing else\n- Preserve all other content exactly as it was\n- Follow the user's instructions precisely and literally\n- Use tools to read, modify, and write files"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Edit the file at `policy.rego`.\n\nAdd a condition to exclude skipped tasks from the deny rule: add 'not task.status == \"Skipped\"' before the result assignment"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I'll read the file, make the requested changes, and save it.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: read_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"policy.rego\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "package example\n\nimport rego.v1\n\ndeny contains result if {\n\tsome task in input.tasks\n\ttask.status != \"Succeeded\"\n\tresult := sprintf(\"Task %s did not succeed\", [task.name])\n}\n", "tool_call_id": "call_67cf2675723f"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Now I'll make the requested changes and save the file.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: write_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"policy.rego\", \"contents\": \"package example\\n\\nimport rego.v1\\n\\ndeny contains result if {\\n\\tsome task in input.tasks\\n\\ttask.status != \\\"Succeeded\\\"\\n\\tnot task.status == \\\"Skipped\\\"\\n\\tresult := sprintf(\\\"Task %s did not succeed\\\", [task.name])\\n}\\n\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "File written successfully.", "tool_call_id": "call_3d2694566eb0"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Done."}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "Your job is to edit files using tools exactly as the user instructs.\n\nYou have access to these tools:\n- `read_file(path)`: Read the contents of a file at the given path\n- `write_file(path, contents)`: Write contents to a file at the given path\n\nCRITICAL GUIDELINES:\n- Do NOT infer or generate content based on file extensions\n- Do NOT create new content that wasn't in the original file\n- Do NOT \"fix\" or \"improve\" the file content\n- Do NOT add domain-specific logic or code\n- ONLY perform the exact text manipulation the user requests\n- If the user says \"replace X with Y\", ONLY replace X with Y - nothing else\n- Preserve all other content exactly as it was\n- Follow the user's instructions precisely and literally\n- Use tools to read, modify, and write files"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Edit the file at `main.py`.\n\nAdd a discount parameter (default 0.0) to calculate_total and apply it to the total before returning"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I'll read the file, make the requested changes, and save it.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: read_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"main.py\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "def calculate_total(items):\n    total = 0\n    for item in items:\n        total += item['price']\n    return total\n", "tool_call_id": "call_1aa5b8e096a1"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Now I'll make the requested changes and save the file.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: write_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"main.py\", \"contents\": \"def calculate_total(items, discount=0.0):\\n    total = 0\\n    for item in items:\\n        total += item['price']\\n    total = total * (1 - discount)\\n    return total\\n\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "File written successfully.", "tool_call_id": "call_7c97f4a20508"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Done."}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "Your job is to edit files using tools exactly as the user instructs.\n\nYou have access to these tools:\n- `read_file(path)`: Read the contents of a file at the given path\n- `write_file(path, contents)`: Write contents to a file at the given path\n\nCRITICAL GUIDELINES:\n- Do NOT infer or generate content based on file extensions\n- Do NOT create new content that wasn't in the original file\n- Do NOT \"fix\" or \"improve\" the file content\n- Do NOT add domain-specific logic or code\n- ONLY perform the exact text manipulation the user requests\n- If the user says \"replace X with Y\", ONLY replace X with Y - nothing else\n- Preserve all other content exactly as it was\n- Follow the user's instructions precisely and literally\n- Use tools to read, modify, and write files"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Edit the file at `client.go`.\n\nAdd error handling to the processData function: return an error if data is empty, and update main to handle the error"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I'll read the file, make the requested changes, and save it.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: read_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"client.go\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "package main\n\nimport \"fmt\"\n\nfunc processData(data string) {\n\tfmt.Println(\"Processing:\", data)\n}\n\nfunc main() {\n\tprocessData(\"test\")\n}\n", "tool_call_id": "call_c198a8d8e058"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Now I'll make the requested changes and save the file.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: write_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"client.go\", \"contents\": \"package main\\n\\nimport \\\"fmt\\\"\\n\\nfunc processData(data string) error {\\n\\tif data == \\\"\\\" {\\n\\t\\treturn fmt.Errorf(\\\"data cannot be empty\\\")\\n\\t}\\n\\tfmt.Println(\\\"Processing:\\\", data)\\n\\treturn nil\\n}\\n\\nfunc main() {\\n\\tif err := processData(\\\"test\\\"); err != nil {\\n\\t\\tfmt.Println(\\\"Error:\\\", err)\\n\\t}\\n}\\n\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "File written successfully.", "tool_call_id": "call_7002f65584d5"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Done."}]}
