{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "Your job is to create and edit files using tools exactly as the user instructs.\n\nYou have access to these tools:\n- `read_file(path)`: Read the contents of a file at the given path\n- `write_file(path, contents)`: Write contents to a file at the given path\n\nGuidelines:\n- Do not infer missing logic\n- Do not create domain-specific content\n- Only create the content the user describes\n- Follow the user's instructions precisely\n- If a file doesn't exist, use write_file to create it"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Create a new file at `script.py` with a simple Go program that prints 'Hello, World!'"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I'll create the new file with the requested content.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: write_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"script.py\", \"contents\": \"package main\\n\\nimport \\\"fmt\\\"\\n\\nfunc main() {\\n\\tfmt.Println(\\\"Hello, World!\\\")\\n}\\n\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "File written successfully.", "tool_call_id": "call_fe40829385fb"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Done. The file has been created."}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "Your job is to edit files using tools exactly as the user instructs.\n\nYou have access to these tools:\n- `read_file(path)`: Read the contents of a file at the given path\n- `write_file(path, contents)`: Write contents to a file at the given path\n\nCRITICAL GUIDELINES:\n- Do NOT infer or generate content based on file extensions\n- Do NOT create new content that wasn't in the original file\n- Do NOT \"fix\" or \"improve\" the file content\n- Do NOT add domain-specific logic or code\n- ONLY perform the exact text manipulation the user requests\n- If the user says \"replace X with Y\", ONLY replace X with Y - nothing else\n- Preserve all other content exactly as it was\n- Follow the user's instructions precisely and literally\n- Use tools to read, modify, and write files"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Edit the file at `README.md`.\n\nUpdate the code block: add a name parameter with default 'World' and use an f-string in the print statement"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I'll read the file, make the requested changes, and save it.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: read_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"README.md\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "# Example\n\nHere's some code:\n\n```python\ndef hello():\n    print(\"Hello\")\n```\n", "tool_call_id": "call_25fbb2eae788"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Now I'll make the requested changes and save the file.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: write_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"README.md\", \"contents\": \"# Example\\n\\nHere's some code:\\n\\n```python\\ndef hello(name=\\\"World\\\"):\\n    print(f\\\"Hello, {name}\\\")\\n```\\n\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "File written successfully.", "tool_call_id": "call_e5c9892b4e18"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Done."}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "Your job is to edit files using tools exactly as the user instructs.\n\nYou have access to these tools:\n- `read_file(path)`: Read the contents of a file at the given path\n- `write_file(path, contents)`: Write contents to a file at the given path\n\nCRITICAL GUIDELINES:\n- Do NOT infer or generate content based on file extensions\n- Do NOT create new content that wasn't in the original file\n- Do NOT \"fix\" or \"improve\" the file content\n- Do NOT add domain-specific logic or code\n- ONLY perform the exact text manipulation the user requests\n- If the user says \"replace X with Y\", ONLY replace X with Y - nothing else\n- Preserve all other content exactly as it was\n- Follow the user's instructions precisely and literally\n- Use tools to read, modify, and write files"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Edit the file at `config.yaml`.\n\nAdd a new 'logging' section with level 'info' and file 'app.log'"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I'll read the file, make the requested changes, and save it.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: read_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"config.yaml\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "server:\n  host: localhost\n  port: 8080\n\ndatabase:\n  name: mydb\n", "tool_call_id": "call_6aa2da6feea7"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Now I'll make the requested changes and save the file.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: write_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"config.yaml\", \"contents\": \"server:\\n  host: localhost\\n  port: 8080\\n\\ndatabase:\\n  name: mydb\\n\\nlogging:\\n  level: info\\n  file: app.log\\n\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "File written successfully.", "tool_call_id": "call_a8e6ccf6b627"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Done."}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "Your job is to edit files using tools exactly as the user instructs.\n\nYou have access to these tools:\n- `read_file(path)`: Read the contents of a file at the given path\n- `write_file(path, contents)`: Write contents to a file at the given path\n\nCRITICAL GUIDELINES:\n- Do NOT infer or generate content based on file extensions\n- Do NOT create new content that wasn't in the original file\n- Do NOT \"fix\" or \"improve\" the file content\n- Do NOT add domain-specific logic or code\n- ONLY perform the exact text manipulation the user requests\n- If the user says \"replace X with Y\", ONLY replace X with Y - nothing else\n- Preserve all other content exactly as it was\n- Follow the user's instructions precisely and literally\n- Use tools to read, modify, and write files"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Edit the file at `sample.txt`.\n\nWrite the following content to the file:\nLine 1: New content\nLine 2: More content"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I'll read the file, make the requested changes, and save it.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: read_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"sample.txt\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "", "tool_call_id": "call_8127eeaa8d41"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Now I'll make the requested changes and save the file.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: write_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"sample.txt\", \"contents\": \"Line 1: New content\\nLine 2: More content\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "File written successfully.", "tool_call_id": "call_18a579e53248"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Done."}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "Your job is to edit files using tools exactly as the user instructs.\n\nYou have access to these tools:\n- `read_file(path)`: Read the contents of a file at the given path\n- `write_file(path, contents)`: Write contents to a file at the given path\n\nCRITICAL GUIDELINES:\n- Do NOT infer or generate content based on file extensions\n- Do NOT create new content that wasn't in the original file\n- Do NOT \"fix\" or \"improve\" the file content\n- Do NOT add domain-specific logic or code\n- ONLY perform the exact text manipulation the user requests\n- If the user says \"replace X with Y\", ONLY replace X with Y - nothing else\n- Preserve all other content exactly as it was\n- Follow the user's instructions precisely and literally\n- Use tools to read, modify, and write files"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Edit the file at `handler.py`.\n\nAdd a discount parameter (default 0.0) to calculate_total and apply it to the total before returning"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I'll read the file, make the requested changes, and save it.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: read_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"handler.py\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "def calculate_total(items):\n    total = 0\n    for item in items:\n        total += item['price']\n    return total\n", "tool_call_id": "call_45e844ec3c7e"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Now I'll make the requested changes and save the file.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: write_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"handler.py\", \"contents\": \"def calculate_total(items, discount=0.0):\\n    total = 0\\n    for item in items:\\n        total += item['price']\\n    total = total * (1 - discount)\\n    return total\\n\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "File written successfully.", "tool_call_id": "call_227faa914b13"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Done."}]}
