{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "Your job is to edit files using tools exactly as the user instructs.\n\nYou have access to these tools:\n- `read_file(path)`: Read the contents of a file at the given path\n- `write_file(path, contents)`: Write contents to a file at the given path\n\nCRITICAL GUIDELINES:\n- Do NOT infer or generate content based on file extensions\n- Do NOT create new content that wasn't in the original file\n- Do NOT \"fix\" or \"improve\" the file content\n- Do NOT add domain-specific logic or code\n- ONLY perform the exact text manipulation the user requests\n- If the user says \"replace X with Y\", ONLY replace X with Y - nothing else\n- Preserve all other content exactly as it was\n- Follow the user's instructions precisely and literally\n- Use tools to read, modify, and write files"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Edit the file at `config.yaml`.\n\n1. Replace 'First line' with 'Updated first line' in line 1\n2. Insert 'Line 2.5: Inserted line' after line 2"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I'll read the file, make the requested changes, and save it.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: read_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"config.yaml\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "Header line\nLine 1: First line\nLine 2: Second line\nLine 3: Third line\nFooter line", "tool_call_id": "call_59faba49bebf"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Now I'll make the requested changes and save the file.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: write_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"config.yaml\", \"contents\": \"Header line\\nLine 1: Updated first line\\nLine 2: Second line\\nLine 2.5: Inserted line\\nLine 3: Third line\\nFooter line\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "File written successfully.", "tool_call_id": "call_58080193f316"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Done."}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "Your job is to edit files using tools exactly as the user instructs.\n\nYou have access to these tools:\n- `read_file(path)`: Read the contents of a file at the given path\n- `write_file(path, contents)`: Write contents to a file at the given path\n\nCRITICAL GUIDELINES:\n- Do NOT infer or generate content based on file extensions\n- Do NOT create new content that wasn't in the original file\n- Do NOT \"fix\" or \"improve\" the file content\n- Do NOT add domain-specific logic or code\n- ONLY perform the exact text manipulation the user requests\n- If the user says \"replace X with Y\", ONLY replace X with Y - nothing else\n- Preserve all other content exactly as it was\n- Follow the user's instructions precisely and literally\n- Use tools to read, modify, and write files"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Edit the file at `app.json`.\n\nAdd a 'description' field with value 'A sample application'"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I'll read the file, make the requested changes, and save it.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: read_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"app.json\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "{\n  \"name\": \"MyApp\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0.0\",\n  \"author\": \"John Doe\"\n}\n", "tool_call_id": "call_f5ef81705b06"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Now I'll make the requested changes and save the file.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: write_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"app.json\", \"contents\": \"{\\n  \\\"name\\\": \\\"MyApp\\\",\\n  \\\"version\\\": \\\"1.0.0\\\",\\n  \\\"author\\\": \\\"John Doe\\\",\\n  \\\"description\\\": \\\"A sample application\\\"\\n}\\n\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "File written successfully.", "tool_call_id": "call_784b0c5ea703"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Done."}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "Your job is to edit files using tools exactly as the user instructs.\n\nYou have access to these tools:\n- `read_file(path)`: Read the contents of a file at the given path\n- `write_file(path, contents)`: Write contents to a file at the given path\n\nCRITICAL GUIDELINES:\n- Do NOT infer or generate content based on file extensions\n- Do NOT create new content that wasn't in the original file\n- Do NOT \"fix\" or \"improve\" the file content\n- Do NOT add domain-specific logic or code\n- ONLY perform the exact text manipulation the user requests\n- If the user says \"replace X with Y\", ONLY replace X with Y - nothing else\n- Preserve all other content exactly as it was\n- Follow the user's instructions precisely and literally\n- Use tools to read, modify, and write files"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Edit the file at `docs.md`.\n\nChange the main heading from 'Introduction' to 'Overview'"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I'll read the file, make the requested changes, and save it.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: read_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"docs.md\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "# Introduction\n\nThis is the introduction section.\n\n## Getting Started\n\nFollow these steps.\n", "tool_call_id": "call_efd769dc74f2"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Now I'll make the requested changes and save the file.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: write_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"docs.md\", \"contents\": \"# Overview\\n\\nThis is the introduction section.\\n\\n## Getting Started\\n\\nFollow these steps.\\n\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "File written successfully.", "tool_call_id": "call_b9aba80bae7e"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Done."}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "Your job is to edit files using tools exactly as the user instructs.\n\nYou have access to these tools:\n- `read_file(path)`: Read the contents of a file at the given path\n- `write_file(path, contents)`: Write contents to a file at the given path\n\nCRITICAL GUIDELINES:\n- Do NOT infer or generate content based on file extensions\n- Do NOT create new content that wasn't in the original file\n- Do NOT \"fix\" or \"improve\" the file content\n- Do NOT add domain-specific logic or code\n- ONLY perform the exact text manipulation the user requests\n- If the user says \"replace X with Y\", ONLY replace X with Y - nothing else\n- Preserve all other content exactly as it was\n- Follow the user's instructions precisely and literally\n- Use tools to read, modify, and write files"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Edit the file at `handler.go`.\n\nAdd error handling to the processData function: return an error if data is empty, and update main to handle the error"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I'll read the file, make the requested changes, and save it.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: read_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"handler.go\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "package main\n\nimport \"fmt\"\n\nfunc processData(data string) {\n\tfmt.Println(\"Processing:\", data)\n}\n\nfunc main() {\n\tprocessData(\"test\")\n}\n", "tool_call_id": "call_db3ea26fee7e"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Now I'll make the requested changes and save the file.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: write_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"handler.go\", \"contents\": \"package main\\n\\nimport \\\"fmt\\\"\\n\\nfunc processData(data string) error {\\n\\tif data == \\\"\\\" {\\n\\t\\treturn fmt.Errorf(\\\"data cannot be empty\\\")\\n\\t}\\n\\tfmt.Println(\\\"Processing:\\\", data)\\n\\treturn nil\\n}\\n\\nfunc main() {\\n\\tif err := processData(\\\"test\\\"); err != nil {\\n\\t\\tfmt.Println(\\\"Error:\\\", err)\\n\\t}\\n}\\n\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "File written successfully.", "tool_call_id": "call_720b9d150fe1"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Done."}]}
