{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "Your job is to edit files using tools exactly as the user instructs.\n\nYou have access to these tools:\n- `read_file(path)`: Read the contents of a file at the given path\n- `write_file(path, contents)`: Write contents to a file at the given path\n\nCRITICAL GUIDELINES:\n- Do NOT infer or generate content based on file extensions\n- Do NOT create new content that wasn't in the original file\n- Do NOT \"fix\" or \"improve\" the file content\n- Do NOT add domain-specific logic or code\n- ONLY perform the exact text manipulation the user requests\n- If the user says \"replace X with Y\", ONLY replace X with Y - nothing else\n- Preserve all other content exactly as it was\n- Follow the user's instructions precisely and literally\n- Use tools to read, modify, and write files"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Edit the file at `settings.yaml`.\n\nUpdate server timeout to 60 and database pool_size to 20"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I'll read the file, make the requested changes, and save it.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: read_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"settings.yaml\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "server:\n  host: localhost\n  port: 8080\n  timeout: 30\n\ndatabase:\n  name: mydb\n  pool_size: 10\n", "tool_call_id": "call_d04280cd7d7e"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Now I'll make the requested changes and save the file.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: write_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"settings.yaml\", \"contents\": \"server:\\n  host: localhost\\n  port: 8080\\n  timeout: 60\\n\\ndatabase:\\n  name: mydb\\n  pool_size: 20\\n\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "File written successfully.", "tool_call_id": "call_784f1cf7b9a3"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Done."}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "Your job is to edit files using tools exactly as the user instructs.\n\nYou have access to these tools:\n- `read_file(path)`: Read the contents of a file at the given path\n- `write_file(path, contents)`: Write contents to a file at the given path\n\nCRITICAL GUIDELINES:\n- Do NOT infer or generate content based on file extensions\n- Do NOT create new content that wasn't in the original file\n- Do NOT \"fix\" or \"improve\" the file content\n- Do NOT add domain-specific logic or code\n- ONLY perform the exact text manipulation the user requests\n- If the user says \"replace X with Y\", ONLY replace X with Y - nothing else\n- Preserve all other content exactly as it was\n- Follow the user's instructions precisely and literally\n- Use tools to read, modify, and write files"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Edit the file at `config.json`.\n\nUpdate the version field to '2.0.0'"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I'll read the file, make the requested changes, and save it.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: read_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"config.json\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "{\n  \"name\": \"MyApp\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0.0\",\n  \"author\": \"John Doe\",\n  \"license\": \"MIT\"\n}\n", "tool_call_id": "call_da286e04087e"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Now I'll make the requested changes and save the file.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: write_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"config.json\", \"contents\": \"{\\n  \\\"name\\\": \\\"MyApp\\\",\\n  \\\"version\\\": \\\"2.0.0\\\",\\n  \\\"author\\\": \\\"John Doe\\\",\\n  \\\"license\\\": \\\"MIT\\\"\\n}\\n\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "File written successfully.", "tool_call_id": "call_8ac143e07370"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Done."}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "Your job is to edit files using tools exactly as the user instructs.\n\nYou have access to these tools:\n- `read_file(path)`: Read the contents of a file at the given path\n- `write_file(path, contents)`: Write contents to a file at the given path\n\nCRITICAL GUIDELINES:\n- Do NOT infer or generate content based on file extensions\n- Do NOT create new content that wasn't in the original file\n- Do NOT \"fix\" or \"improve\" the file content\n- Do NOT add domain-specific logic or code\n- ONLY perform the exact text manipulation the user requests\n- If the user says \"replace X with Y\", ONLY replace X with Y - nothing else\n- Preserve all other content exactly as it was\n- Follow the user's instructions precisely and literally\n- Use tools to read, modify, and write files"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Edit the file at `config.yaml`.\n\nReplace lines 3-4 with:\nLine 3: Updated third line\nLine 4: Updated fourth line"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I'll read the file, make the requested changes, and save it.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: read_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"config.yaml\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "Line 1: First line\nLine 2: Second line\nLine 3: Third line\nLine 4: Fourth line\nLine 5: Fifth line", "tool_call_id": "call_277b39207dcc"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Now I'll make the requested changes and save the file.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: write_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"config.yaml\", \"contents\": \"Line 1: First line\\nLine 2: Second line\\nLine 3: Updated third line\\nLine 4: Updated fourth line\\nLine 5: Fifth line\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "File written successfully.", "tool_call_id": "call_736a9a34d0a0"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Done."}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "Your job is to edit files using tools exactly as the user instructs.\n\nYou have access to these tools:\n- `read_file(path)`: Read the contents of a file at the given path\n- `write_file(path, contents)`: Write contents to a file at the given path\n\nCRITICAL GUIDELINES:\n- Do NOT infer or generate content based on file extensions\n- Do NOT create new content that wasn't in the original file\n- Do NOT \"fix\" or \"improve\" the file content\n- Do NOT add domain-specific logic or code\n- ONLY perform the exact text manipulation the user requests\n- If the user says \"replace X with Y\", ONLY replace X with Y - nothing else\n- Preserve all other content exactly as it was\n- Follow the user's instructions precisely and literally\n- Use tools to read, modify, and write files"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Edit the file at `main.go`.\n\nAdd the 'time' package to imports and print the current time in main"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I'll read the file, make the requested changes, and save it.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: read_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"main.go\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "package main\n\nimport \"fmt\"\n\nfunc main() {\n\tfmt.Println(\"Hello\")\n}\n", "tool_call_id": "call_53958130ccb9"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Now I'll make the requested changes and save the file.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: write_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"main.go\", \"contents\": \"package main\\n\\nimport (\\n\\t\\\"fmt\\\"\\n\\t\\\"time\\\"\\n)\\n\\nfunc main() {\\n\\tfmt.Println(\\\"Hello\\\")\\n\\tfmt.Println(\\\"Time:\\\", time.Now())\\n}\\n\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "File written successfully.", "tool_call_id": "call_dcd87d361a0f"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Done."}]}
