{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "Your job is to edit files using tools exactly as the user instructs.\n\nYou have access to these tools:\n- `read_file(path)`: Read the contents of a file at the given path\n- `write_file(path, contents)`: Write contents to a file at the given path\n\nCRITICAL GUIDELINES:\n- Do NOT infer or generate content based on file extensions\n- Do NOT create new content that wasn't in the original file\n- Do NOT \"fix\" or \"improve\" the file content\n- Do NOT add domain-specific logic or code\n- ONLY perform the exact text manipulation the user requests\n- If the user says \"replace X with Y\", ONLY replace X with Y - nothing else\n- Preserve all other content exactly as it was\n- Follow the user's instructions precisely and literally\n- Use tools to read, modify, and write files"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Edit the file at `example.txt`.\n\nReplace the paragraph starting with 'Foo' with: 'This is the new paragraph content.'"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I'll read the file, make the requested changes, and save it.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: read_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"example.txt\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "Introduction paragraph\nThis is a long paragraph starting with 'Foo' that contains\nmultiple lines of text that need to be replaced.\nThe paragraph continues here.\nEnd of paragraph\nConclusion paragraph", "tool_call_id": "call_94b6de1fdb1f"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Now I'll make the requested changes and save the file.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: write_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"example.txt\", \"contents\": \"Introduction paragraph\\nThis is the new paragraph content.\\nConclusion paragraph\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "File written successfully.", "tool_call_id": "call_bd1841a5c782"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Done."}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "Your job is to edit files using tools exactly as the user instructs.\n\nYou have access to these tools:\n- `read_file(path)`: Read the contents of a file at the given path\n- `write_file(path, contents)`: Write contents to a file at the given path\n\nCRITICAL GUIDELINES:\n- Do NOT infer or generate content based on file extensions\n- Do NOT create new content that wasn't in the original file\n- Do NOT \"fix\" or \"improve\" the file content\n- Do NOT add domain-specific logic or code\n- ONLY perform the exact text manipulation the user requests\n- If the user says \"replace X with Y\", ONLY replace X with Y - nothing else\n- Preserve all other content exactly as it was\n- Follow the user's instructions precisely and literally\n- Use tools to read, modify, and write files"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Edit the file at `utils.py`.\n\nAdd a discount parameter (default 0.0) to calculate_total and apply it to the total before returning"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I'll read the file, make the requested changes, and save it.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: read_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"utils.py\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "def calculate_total(items):\n    total = 0\n    for item in items:\n        total += item['price']\n    return total\n", "tool_call_id": "call_dcb6c528bd13"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Now I'll make the requested changes and save the file.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: write_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"utils.py\", \"contents\": \"def calculate_total(items, discount=0.0):\\n    total = 0\\n    for item in items:\\n        total += item['price']\\n    total = total * (1 - discount)\\n    return total\\n\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "File written successfully.", "tool_call_id": "call_29f2e673d03b"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Done."}]}
