{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "Your job is to edit files using tools exactly as the user instructs.\n\nYou have access to these tools:\n- `read_file(path)`: Read the contents of a file at the given path\n- `write_file(path, contents)`: Write contents to a file at the given path\n\nCRITICAL GUIDELINES:\n- Do NOT infer or generate content based on file extensions\n- Do NOT create new content that wasn't in the original file\n- Do NOT \"fix\" or \"improve\" the file content\n- Do NOT add domain-specific logic or code\n- ONLY perform the exact text manipulation the user requests\n- If the user says \"replace X with Y\", ONLY replace X with Y - nothing else\n- Preserve all other content exactly as it was\n- Follow the user's instructions precisely and literally\n- Use tools to read, modify, and write files"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Edit the file at `input.txt`.\n\nReplace the line starting with 'Config option 2' with 'Config option 2: new_value'"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I'll read the file, make the requested changes, and save it.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: read_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"input.txt\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "Config option 1: value1\nConfig option 2: value2\nConfig option 3: value3\nOther line", "tool_call_id": "call_0702a1e213cf"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Now I'll make the requested changes and save the file.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: write_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"input.txt\", \"contents\": \"Config option 1: value1\\nConfig option 2: new_value\\nConfig option 3: value3\\nOther line\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "File written successfully.", "tool_call_id": "call_51bbb098bf50"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Done."}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "Your job is to edit files using tools exactly as the user instructs.\n\nYou have access to these tools:\n- `read_file(path)`: Read the contents of a file at the given path\n- `write_file(path, contents)`: Write contents to a file at the given path\n\nCRITICAL GUIDELINES:\n- Do NOT infer or generate content based on file extensions\n- Do NOT create new content that wasn't in the original file\n- Do NOT \"fix\" or \"improve\" the file content\n- Do NOT add domain-specific logic or code\n- ONLY perform the exact text manipulation the user requests\n- If the user says \"replace X with Y\", ONLY replace X with Y - nothing else\n- Preserve all other content exactly as it was\n- Follow the user's instructions precisely and literally\n- Use tools to read, modify, and write files"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Edit the file at `utils.py`.\n\nImport datetime and update get_date to return the current date using datetime.now()"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I'll read the file, make the requested changes, and save it.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: read_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"utils.py\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "def get_date():\n    return \"2024-01-01\"\n", "tool_call_id": "call_2565ee39bf09"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Now I'll make the requested changes and save the file.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: write_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"utils.py\", \"contents\": \"from datetime import datetime\\n\\ndef get_date():\\n    return datetime.now().strftime(\\\"%Y-%m-%d\\\")\\n\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "File written successfully.", "tool_call_id": "call_da0c2cf96d6b"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Done."}]}
